scenario_id: dpgd-116
theme: hogans-heroes
run_id: 2
total_caught: 4
total_findings: 7
weighted_caught: 23
total_weight: 37
score_pct: 62.2
findings:
- finding_id: C1
  title: from_file_or_default swallows ALL errors including parse and permission failures
  weight: 8
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: 'Reviewer F3 flags: ''Config silently ignores missing file when explicitly
    specified... std::fs::read_to_string(path) failure is swallowed with if let Ok(contents).
    An explicitly-specified config path that doesn''t exist is almost certainly an
    operator mistake.'' TEA also listed ''silent error swallowing prevention'' in
    security test coverage.'
- finding_id: I1
  title: CliError Display leaks internal details to stderr (CWE-209)
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: dev
  evidence: 'Reviewer V2 verifies: ''CliError Display impls use generic messages ("server
    error", "access denied") and do NOT echo inner String payloads... The /// **SECURITY:**
    comment is present. The test at security.rs:17-33 confirms this.'' Dev implemented
    CWE-209 safe Display.'
- finding_id: I2
  title: "SiemClient.tenant_id uses raw String \u2014 header injection risk (CWE-113)"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: "Pipeline caught CRLF header injection via validate_header_value() (Reviewer\
    \ V1), but the finding is about using raw String instead of validated TenantId\
    \ from axiathon-core. No phase flagged the type-safety gap \u2014 tenant_id remains\
    \ a plain String, bypassing the newtype pattern required by SOUL.md principle\
    \ #2."
- finding_id: I3
  title: Dependencies use direct version strings instead of workspace = true
  weight: 3
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: Reviewer V7 says 'Workspace dependencies are declared centrally' but does
    not check whether individual crate Cargo.toml uses workspace = true vs direct
    version strings. The code changes show Cargo.toml modifications but no phase flagged
    the 6 deps using direct versions.
- finding_id: I4
  title: "Config token field silently ignored \u2014 secret left on disk"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: 'Reviewer F4 explicitly: ''ConfigFile derives Deserialize without #[serde(deny_unknown_fields)].
    Writing token = "should-be-ignored" in the config file is silently accepted. Typos
    like servel_url instead of server_url are silently ignored.'''
- finding_id: I5
  title: "Vacuously true test \u2014 assertion is None || true"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: "Reviewer F7 flags vacuous test assertions: 'config_loading.rs:219-222:\
    \ assert!(config.is_ok() || config.is_err()) \u2014 always true, asserts nothing\
    \ meaningful.' Same pattern as the is_none() || true finding \u2014 reviewer identified\
    \ the category of vacuous OR assertions."
- finding_id: I6
  title: "Test with zero assertions \u2014 only checks non-panic"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: Reviewer F7 flagged tautologies and unchecked parameters but did not identify
    the specific zero-assertion test using 'let _ = config' with no assert_eq! checks
    on server() and token(). The specific test pattern of checking only non-panic
    was not called out.
